\name{cellucid_history_diff}
\alias{cellucid_history_diff}
\title{Compare two steps}
\usage{
cellucid_history_diff(viewer, a, b)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{a}{The first step. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{step}}{A step, by its id (history_get lists the steps). Text. Required.}\item{\code{tracker}}{A tracker by its name or its id (history_summary lists them); the tracker in use when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Optional.}}}
\item{b}{The second step. A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{step}}{A step, by its id (history_get lists the steps). Text. Required.}\item{\code{tracker}}{A tracker by its name or its id (history_summary lists them); the tracker in use when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Optional.}}}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{a}, \code{b}, \code{common} (Their last common step (null across trackers)), \code{domains}. Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
What differs between the state after two steps, part by part (filters, labels, highlights, \ldots); the steps may be of two trackers.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.diff} (History). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
